{
  "archive": "tddft.qvf",
  "description": "Water TD-DFT: an excited_states table of three singlet states (B1, A2, A1) with excitation energies in eV and total energies in hartree, oscillator strengths whose transition dipoles (atomic units) satisfy f = (2/3) dE |mu|^2, zero rotatory strengths, magnetic transition dipoles, and orbital contributions indexing the 7-orbital ground-state wavefunction that wavefunction_ref names. State 1 names its hole NTO section (nto_ref; the particle section carries the same state_ref and state_index with nto_role particle, occupations are the pair weights) and its volume.transition_density (density_ref; the volume names the state back with excited_states_ref and state_index). The spectra.uvvis stick spectrum has one line per state at its excitation energy with the oscillator strength as intensity, and its peaks name states by state_index through states_ref (spec \u00a7 5.2, \u00a7 5.3, \u00a7 5.4, \u00a7 5.12).",
